# Response headers for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages (both read this file from the published folder).
# COOP + COEP make the page cross-origin isolated, which enables SharedArrayBuffer and so the multithreaded
# RAW decoder. Every resource Tintwork loads is same-origin, so require-corp blocks nothing it uses.
# Without these headers (for example on GitHub Pages) Tintwork falls back to the single-threaded decoder.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
